WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.435 --> 00:00:04.280
Acerina and the Rock That Held Up the Sky

2
00:00:05.115 --> 00:00:11.215
In Benahoare, the island we now call La
Palma, Acerina looked up whenever she

3
00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:12.420
entered the Caldera.

4
00:00:12.855 --> 00:00:17.220
There stood Idafe, a great rock that
seemed to hold up the sky.

5
00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:22.740
One morning, she went with her grandfather
and other people from the village.

6
00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:27.295
They carried small pots of food for an
ancient ceremony.

7
00:00:27.295 --> 00:00:32.955
Her grandfather explained that this place
was connected with Abora and the memory of

8
00:00:32.955 --> 00:00:33.955
their ancestors.

9
00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:38.760
When they arrived, they all said: “Idafe
still stands;

10
00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:40.880
we keep its memory alive.”

11
00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:44.140
Suddenly, the ground trembled.

12
00:00:44.615 --> 00:00:49.115
Several stones tumbled down the slope, and
Acerina thought the rock was going to

13
00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:54.860
fall. Her grandfather took her hand, and
the group moved away from the cliff.

14
00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:56.800
The noise stopped.

15
00:00:57.555 --> 00:01:01.260
Idafe still stood tall against the sky.

16
00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:08.155
Acerina left her pot in the place she was
shown and promised to learn the words of

17
00:01:08.155 --> 00:01:11.120
the ceremony so that they would not be
forgotten.

18
00:01:11.975 --> 00:01:13.380
The years passed.

19
00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:17.040
Acerina became a gifted storyteller.

20
00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:23.035
She took the children to a safe spot where
they could look at the rock, and told them

21
00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:24.620
what she had experienced.

22
00:01:25.315 --> 00:01:31.600
At the end, they all looked at the stone
and repeated: “Idafe still stands;

23
00:01:32.275 --> 00:01:33.880
we keep its memory alive.”

